@model ReformedHistory.Views.Content.Confessions.Secret.SecretSection

<h2 id="@this.Model.Link">Chapter @this.Model.Index</h2>
<h3>@this.Model.Name</h3>
<br />

<div class="centerQuote">
    <span>
        No theologian of sound judgment from the reformed church wishes to deny a general 
        intention or ordination concerning the salvation of each and every person by the death 
        of Christ, on this condition: if he will believe.
    </span>
    <span>Bishop John Davenant, Response to the French Reformed Churches</span>
</div>
    
<ol>
    <li>
        Through His life, ministry, and obedience to the law, Christ became the perfect sacrifice to atone for
        the sins of humanity. He also became the perfect high priest to offer Himself to the Father.
    </li>
    <li>
        Christ was pierced for the transgressions of sinners, and His death paid the debt that was
        due for sin. Through His death, Christ defeated sin, death, the devil, and the powers of Hell.
    </li>
    <li>
        Christ's atonement is infinite in value, more than sufficient to redeem each and every person in the world.
    </li>
    <li>
        Faith is required to participate in Christ's death, so the atonement is only efficient for those who believe.
    </li>
    <!--<li>
        Through the atonement, God establishes the well-meant offer of the gospel: all who have faith
        shall not perish but have eternal life.
    </li>-->
</ol>
<br />